<p>Ukraine shot down more than 33,000 Russian drones of various types in March using interceptor systems, a monthly record since Russia launched its full-scale invasion more than four years ago, Defense Minister Mykhailo Fedorov said. Fedorov said Ukraine was increasing supplies of interceptor drones to counter Russian air attacks and had created a new command within the air force to strengthen those efforts. Ukraine’s Defense Ministry said Tuesday that the country’s long-range strike capability has increased from 630 km to 1,750 km since Russia’s February 2022 invasion, enabling strikes on Russian oil facilities and factories supplying Moscow’s armed forces. Ukraine’s Unmanned Systems Forces said Ukrainian forces struck Russian oil facilities at the Black Sea port of Tuapse for the third time this month, while Russia’s Defense Ministry said its air defenses intercepted 186 Ukrainian drones overnight across Russian regions, Crimea, the Black Sea and the Sea of Azov. Newsis said it could not independently verify the competing battlefield claims.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kts7xrlzpTg1aqb316eVJQ4S7rk_kTKBIqHIiLchNI2xFPYEyDkHdNSyzlsurgFtJ2al6BNwVS_UE30flXjYQDOiI37YJiWCIZkqDlW4Dp2mIKoqtYaxKqzi0OaW30EaILUewPazXNe8TMlSqsfgQv2FH1d2J0oQxNOYOFkobghgbJEuyrM78mgpXCk6SgvK74DA7A' alt='Image accompanying coverage of Ukraine’s claim that it downed 33,000 Russian drones in March.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Procurement surge: Over the past four months, Ukrainian forces received twice as many interceptor drones through the Defense Procurement Agency and the State Operator for Rear as they received in all of the previous year, United24 Media reported, citing Suspilne News.</li><li>Foreign demand: Ukrainian officials said interceptor drones are drawing interest from Middle Eastern and Gulf countries during the Iran war.</li><li>Oil targets: Ukraine’s Unmanned Systems Forces said two earlier attacks this month on Tuapse destroyed 24 oil storage tanks and damaged four others.</li><li>Tuapse operation: Ukraine said several defense and security-service units took part in the latest strike on the Black Sea port.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukraine’s Defense Minister Mykhailo Fedorov: Fedorov said Ukraine was expanding interceptor-drone supplies and had created a new air force command to improve air-defense capabilities. (<a href='https://www.mediafax.ro/stirile-zilei/ucraina-declara-ca-a-doborat-33-000-de-drone-rusesti-in-martie-stabilind-un-record-lunar-23728056'>Mediafax</a>)</li><li>Ukraine’s Defense Ministry: The ministry said Ukraine’s long-range strike reach had grown from 630 km to 1,750 km since February 2022, allowing strikes on oil facilities and factories tied to Russia’s war effort. (<a href='https://www.newsis.com/view/NISX20260428_0003610290'>Newsis</a>)</li><li>Russia’s Defense Ministry: The ministry said Russian air defenses intercepted 186 Ukrainian drones overnight across Russian regions, Crimea, the Black Sea and the Sea of Azov. (<a href='https://www.newsis.com/view/NISX20260428_0003610290'>Newsis</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1sxycbd/ukraine_says_it_shot_down_33000_russian_drones_in/'>Ukraine says it shot down 33,000 Russian drones in March, a monthly record</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3351755/ukraine-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-1-month-defence-minister'>Ukraine shot down 33,000 Russian drones in 1 month: defence minister</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ukraine-says-it-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-in-march-monthly-record/article70916306.ece'>Ukraine says it shot down 33,000 Russian drones in March, monthly record</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.military.com/daily-news/2026/04/28/ukraine-says-it-shot-down-33000-russian-drones-march-monthly-record.html'>Ukraine Says It Shot Down 33,000 Russian Drones in March, 